# Workspace preset names, per naming profile (owner directive 12.1).
#
# One row per CANONICAL id, three whitespace-separated columns:
#
#     <canonical id>    <legacy name>    <modern name>
#
# The canonical id is the identity and NEVER changes, whatever either column
# says or how the thing is displayed. It is what `.mhm` and workspace files
# persist, so a file written under one profile opens under the other.
#
# LEGACY is the default profile. `--naming modern` opts in, and either
# profile still accepts the other's names -- with a warning the first time --
# so old- and new-named things coexist in one workspace.
#
# Names may not contain whitespace; the parser refuses a row that is not
# exactly three fields rather than guessing where a name ends.

workspace.modelling    Modelling    Modelling
workspace.rigging      Rigging      Rigging

# The rename the owner asked for. The dock itself became "Assets" on
# 2026-09-07 -- `TaskRegistry::add(id, title)` split identity from label -- and
# this is the preset catching up. The canonical id says "assets" because that
# is what the layout is FOR; the legacy column keeps the CLI argument that has
# always worked.
workspace.assets       Materials    Assets

workspace.export       Export       Export
workspace.tabbed       Tabbed       Tabbed
